   "source": {
    "label": "th:flat-lip",
    "number": "Theorem (th:flat-lip)",
    "quote": "If ContextualExp3 is run in the bandit feedback model with parameter $\\ve = (\\ln T)^{\\frac{2}{p+d+2}}\\,T^{-\\frac{1}{p+d+2}}$, then its regret $\\Reg_T(\\cF)$ with respect to the set $\\cF$ of $1$-Lipschitz functions $f : \\cX\\to\\cY$ satisfies $\\Reg_T(\\cF) = {\\tilde \\cO}\\big(T^\\frac{p+d+1}{p+d+2}\\big)$, where the ${\\tilde \\cO}$ notation hides factors polynomial in $C_{\\cX}$ and $C_{\\cY}$, and $\\ln T$ factors."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Paper describes this as a known result (cf. Slivkins 2014) proven as warmup; marked is_new=false but kept as the paper states and proves it. Regret is E[sum losses] - inf_f sum losses, i.e. expected regret vs best policy in hindsight with oblivious adversary."
  },
